<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#coyotlatelco">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Coyotlatelco</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 600–900</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Also known as Coyotlatelco culture</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Coyotlatelco is a style of red-on-buff pottery, and by extension the archaeological culture associated with it, found in the Basin of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a> in the centuries after the decline of Teotihuacan, roughly 600 to 900 CE. Its appearance among the ruins of Teotihuacan and in new settlements marks a period of political fragmentation and probably the arrival of new populations in central Mexico.</p></div>
